  "description": "ZIDTEO crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C136 H104 Dy4 N12 O22. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.536-3.867 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.54-112.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C136H104Dy4N12O22. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
